#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
# kawa-fixer — the update's local AI fixer (.claude/notes/update-design.md §4.5, T47): when an update
# makes a program refuse a config file of ours, an open-weight model on this PC's own graphics card
# proposes the smallest edit, and only what the program's own check then takes is kept. No cloud, no
# keys, loaded only during a run; everything it cannot do ends in "held + told".
#
# What keeps it harmless: the model has no tools. Text goes in, one JSON answer comes out (its form
# forced by a grammar), and this program alone reads it: exact search/replace edits on the config
# files of the program at fault, nothing else — never a command, never another file. Every edit
# passes the guard rails (validate) before it is tried, on a copy of the system (the updater's
# candidate), and the checks it must pass are out of its reach. Two tries; then the package waits.
#
#   kawa-fixer run CASE.json [--out OUT.json] [--sock SOCK] [--log DIR]   one failure, the whole loop
#   kawa-fixer keep OUT.json --fixes DIR              a proven fix recorded (the updater's memory)
#   kawa-fixer reapply --fixes DIR --home HOME [--root /]   the kept fixes on freshly themed configs
#   kawa-fixer serve --sock SOCK [--model FILE]       the model alone, in the foreground (the bench)
#   kawa-fixer status [--full] [--home HOME]          ready, or what is missing (--full: the hashes)
#   kawa-fixer install [--home HOME]                  the runtime and the model, into ~/.local
# Exit: 0 fixed / done · 3 held (OUT.json says why) · 2 misuse
#
# CASE.json, written by the updater (lib/fixer.sh) or the bench (tools/fixer-bench.py):
#   why       the red lines of the checks        packages  [{name, old, new}] what was held
#   runner    argv prefix: a command as the desktop's user in the candidate, HOME set, no display
#   home      that HOME as this program reaches it · root  the candidate's / as this program reaches
#             it · old_root  the system before it (the docs' old text; "/" in the updater)
#   home_in   HOME as the runner sees it         budget_s  the wall clock for the whole case
